{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527507346,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzMjY5OTYxOTM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2576","origin":"github"},"title":"Option to store run records in annexed sidecar files","message":"Here is a scenario that might always lead to leakage of private information into a run record (TL;DR: identifying information somewhere in the path names): https://github.com/psychoinformatics-de/datalad-hirni/issues/16\n\nAs a general solution to the issue of sensitive information in file names (in subdatasets, that could be detached and stay private) with respect to leakage in run records, it would be nice to be able to GPG-encrypt run records.\n\nThere is already a place for the necessary config in git: `user.signingkey=...` so we could use that too.\n\n`re-run` would then need to decrypt on-access.\n\n@kyleam @yarikoptic","files":null}]}